# Novie: which browser opens a link or an HTML file.
#
# Without this file nothing in the guest states a preference, and GIO falls back to the first
# entry in /usr/share/applications/mimeinfo.cache -- which is alphabetical, so the answer
# depends on which browsers happen to be installed. With Firefox alone that was Firefox by
# default; adding Chromium silently moved it, and only for the paths that go through
# xdg-open or GIO (a link clicked in Thunar, an app that shells out). The XFCE panel's own
# Web Browser button never consults this at all -- it asks exo, which reads helpers.rc -- so
# the two could disagree without either being configured. They are both pointed at Chromium
# here and in ~novie/.config/xfce4/helpers.rc.
#
# This is the system default from the XDG mime-apps spec: a user's own
# ~/.config/mimeapps.list still overrides it, and it merges with what the packages registered
# rather than replacing it (unlike an xfconf channel file in /etc/xdg, see AGENTS.md).
[Default Applications]
x-scheme-handler/http=chromium.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=chromium.desktop
text/html=chromium.desktop
application/xhtml+xml=chromium.desktop
